<title>USA: Citadel Holding Q2 shr $0.06 vs $0.69.</title>
<headline>Citadel Holding Q2 shr $0.06 vs $0.69.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					  June 30,	    June 30,</p>
<p>				  1997     1996	    1997    1996</p>
<p>	    (In thousands of dollars, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>				  1,387   1,572	   2,605   3,312</p>
<p>Gain on sale of rental property</p>
<p>				     --   1,473	    (16)   1,473</p>
<p>Losses of and Write-Down</p>
<p>of Investment in Fidelity</p>
<p>  Federal Bank		   --   4,000		--   4,000</p>
<p>Earnings before income taxes</p>
<p>				    428   5,541	     704   5,784</p>
<p>Income tax expense (benefit)</p>
<p>				     15	--		45	--</p>
<p> Net Earnings		   413   5,541	     659   5,784</p>
<p>Earnings per common and common</p>
<p>  equivalent share	   0.06    0.69	    0.10    0.72</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Citadel Holding Corp.</p>
<p>The one-time gain of $1.49 million for the three and six months is from the sale of an apartment building and a parcel of land, while the $4.0 million in income came from the sale of loans and properties from the company's former unit, Fidelity Federal Bank.</p>
